[["\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 51975 and 68962?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of **51,975** and **68,962** step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 51,975 by 2 (ones place of 68,962):**\n   \\[\n   51,\\!975 \\times 2 = 103,\\!950\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 51,975 by 60 (tens place of 68,962):**\n   \\[\n   51,\\!975 \\times 60 = 3,\\!118,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 51,975 by 900 (hundreds place of 68,962):**\n   \\[\n   51,\\!975 \\times 900 = 46,\\!777,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 51,975 by 8,000 (thousands place of 68,962):**\n   \\[\n   51,\\!975 \\times 8,\\!000 = 415,\\!800,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 51,975 by 60,000 (ten-thousands place of 68,962):**\n   \\[\n   51,\\!975 \\times 60,\\!000 = 3,\\!118,\\!500,\\!000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n103,\\!950 + 3,\\!118,\\!500 + 46,\\!777,\\!500 + 415,\\!800,\\!000 + 3,\\!118,\\!500,\\!000 = 3,\\!584,\\!300,\\!000\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{3,\\!584,\\!300,\\!000}\\).", "\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 51,975 and 68,962. To do this, I'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts by considering each digit of the second number and its place value.\n\nStarting with the ones place, I'll multiply 51,975 by 2. This gives me 103,950.\n\nNext, I'll move to the tens place. Here, I'll multiply 51,975 by 60, which equals 3,118,500.\n\nThen, I'll handle the hundreds place by multiplying 51,975 by 900. This results in 46,777,500.\n\nAfter that, I'll address the thousands place by multiplying 51,975 by 8,000, giving me 415,800,000.\n\nFinally, I'll consider the ten-thousands place by multiplying 51,975 by 60,000, which equals 3,118,500,000.\n\nNow, I'll add all these partial products together to find the total sum. Adding them step by step:\n\n103,950 + 3,118,500 = 3,222,450\n\n3,222,450 + 46,777,500 = 50,000,000\n\n50,000,000 + 415,800,000 = 465,800,000\n\n465,800,000 + 3,118,500,000 = 3,584,300,000\n\nSo, the final product of 51,975 and 68,962 is 3,584,300,000.\n"]]
